[{:seon.task/name "the-record-is-an-atom"
  :seon.task/plan "The agent's record is one map it reads with @ctx (seon.ctx/ctx; notes/design-ctx-atom-2026-10-25.md, the owner's rulings of 2026-10-25). What exists: an agent reads its record through my.db queries and my.task functions, each a read of its own; the page draws its agent from the walk (seon.render/walk). The first slice (the owner, 2026-10-25: \"just deref'ing the @ctx will trigger the web ui rendering which the agent will also see so focus on the rendering functions part\"): seon.ctx builds the agent entity whole and its units (:seon.render/units) by short keys once, when the agent's state first holds its db, and patches it from each transaction's datoms (seon.agent/transact! records them), so a read is a deref and a write costs its change. The model reads @ctx through the one printer as any value; the page draws the same eval as a block (:seon.ctx/ctx, seon.render.ui/ctx), each key by the render its own schema declares, so an agent adds a datum and its render and sees both at its next eval. Writes through swap! (the validator, the basis check), provenance, the diff from main and its merge mark follow, each its own step of the note's plan."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx-test/ctx-is-the-record-after-every-transaction seon.ctx-test/the-patch-costs-the-change-not-the-session seon.ctx-test/a-key-renders-by-its-own-schema seon.ctx-test/an-agent-adds-a-datum-and-its-render seon.ctx-test/the-agents-state-keeps-ctx seon.agent-test/a-parked-agent-draws-its-own-render-and-a-gone-one-answers-at-once seon.ctx-test/a-swap-writes-the-record seon.ctx-test/a-write-costs-its-change-not-the-record}}]
